"50">18&#x02009;700 (15&#x02009;500, 23&#x02009;400)</td><td align="center" valign="top" charoff="50">20&#x02009;800 (17&#x02009;200, 26&#x02009;000)</td></tr><tr><td align="left" valign="top" charoff="50">&#x02003;50&#x00025; coverage</td><td align="center" valign="top" charoff="50">3900 (3200, 4900)</td><td align="center" valign="top" charoff="50">8900 (7400, 11&#x02009;200)</td><td align="center" valign="top" charoff="50">10&#x02009;300 (8600, 12&#x02009;900)</td></tr><tr><td align="left" valign="top" charoff="50">&#x000a0;</td><td align="center" valign="top" charoff="50">&#x000a0;</td><td align="center" valign="top" charoff="50">&#x000a0;</td><td align="center" valign="top" charoff="50">&#x000a0;</td></tr><tr><td align="left" valign="top" charoff="50"><italic>Bayesian model</italic></td><td align="center" valign="top" charoff="50">&#x000a0;</td><td align="center" valign="top" charoff="50">&#x000a0;</td><td align="center" valign="top" charoff="50">&#x000a0;</td></tr><tr><td align="left" valign="top" charoff="50">&#x02003;100&#x00025; coverage</td><td align="center" valign="top" charoff="50">17&#x02009;900 (14&#x02009;900, 22&#x02009;400)</td><td align="center" valign="top" charoff="50">29&#x02009;300 (24&#x02009;200, 36&#x02009;600)</td><td align="center" valign="top" charoff="50">32&#x02009;800 (27&#x02009;200, 41&#x02009;000)</td></tr><tr><td align="left" valign="top" charoff="50">&#x02003;75&#x00025; coverage</td><td align="center" valign="top" charoff="50">11&#x02009;000 (9100, 13&#x02009;700)</td><td align="center" valign="top" charoff="50">18&#x02009;800 (15&#x02009;600, 23&#x02009;500)</td><td align="center" valign="top" charoff="50">20&#x02009;900 (17&#x02009;300, 26&#x02009;100)</td></tr><tr><td align="left" valign="top" charoff="50">&#x02003;50&#x00025; coverage</td><td align="center" valign="top" charoff="50">4000 (3300, 5000)</td><td align="center" valign="top" charoff="50">9000 (7500, 11&#x02009;300)</td><td align="center" valign="top" charoff="50">10&#x02009;100 (8400, 12&#x02009;600)</td></tr></tbody></table><table-wrap-foot><fn id="tbfnote1"><label/><p>Numbers are rounded to the nearest hundred. Ranges (in parentheses) around the point estimates were calculated by varying the percentage change in future period and cohort effects per 5-year time period from &#x02212;5 to 5&#x00025; over the base case values. A &#x02212;5&#x00025; change in both period and cohort effects yielded an overall percentage change of &#x02212;17.2&#x00025;, while a &#x0002b;5&#x00025; change in both period and cohort effects resulted in an overall percentage change of &#x0002b;25.0&#x00025; over the 15-year projected period.</p></fn></table-wrap-foot></table-wrap></floats-wrap></article>